item.text:
Counts: candidates discovered about 34, promising docs opened 18, accepted units 10, duplicates/near-duplicates 17, context-only items 7, inaccessible items 3.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"\"I Will Take My Percentage\": Congolese Presidential Adviser Caught on Tape Negotiating Corrupt Mineral Deal","publisher":"OCCRP","publication_date":"2022-09-15","url":"https://www.occrp.org/en/investigation/i-will-take-my-percentage-congolese-presidential-adviser-caught-on-tape-negotiating-corrupt-mineral-deal","claim":"A covert-recording investigation showed Vidiye Tshimanga, one of Tshisekedi's closest advisers, offering to help investors win mining licenses and cut red tape in exchange for a stake, while describing ways to hide his share through proxies and offshore trusts.","locator":"lines 40-74","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"The claim is supported by direct recordings, named participants, and in-article confirmation that the meetings occurred.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target period and tied to Tshisekedi's inner-circle network.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong: the conduct is by a close presidential adviser using proximity to Tshisekedi and claiming access through him.","contrary_evidence":["Tshimanga denied wrongdoing and said the statements were taken out of context","the video-makers were unidentified"],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.4","7B.5","7B.9","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Top Congo presidential adviser resigns after allegedly requesting bribe on tape","publisher":"Reuters","publication_date":"2022-09-16","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/top-congo-presidential-adviser-resigns-after-allegedly-requested-bribe-on-tape-2894087","claim":"Reuters reported that Tshimanga resigned after being caught on tape negotiating a corrupt mineral deal, and that Tshisekedi's communications director said the fight against corruption is one of the president's pillars and that anyone in the Office of the President who violated the law would suffer the consequences.","locator":"lines 418-431","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous wire reporting with a direct presidency response and no dependence on a single anonymous source family.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 target period.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to the president's office response; the underlying misconduct is by a close adviser in Tshisekedi's cabinet.","contrary_evidence":["Tshimanga denied wrongdoing","the statement did not name Tshimanga"],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC : ouverture d'une information judiciaire à l'encontre de Vidiye Tshimanga","publisher":"Radio Okapi","publication_date":"2022-09-20","url":"https://www.radiookapi.net/2022/09/20/actualite/justice/rdc-ouverture-dune-information-judiciaire-lencontre-de-vidiye-tshimanga","claim":"The Kinshasa-Gombe prosecutor opened a judicial inquiry into former special adviser Vidiye Tshimanga and asked him to answer questions after the corruption allegations aired publicly in September 2022.","locator":"lines 148-150","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Local outlet reporting a formal prosecutorial step in direct response to the recorded allegations.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 target period.","ruler_attribution":"Strong on the office network: the inquiry targeted a former special adviser to Tshisekedi, not an abstract national corruption climate.","contrary_evidence":["The article reports allegations before final judgment","Tshimanga denied the accusations"],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Que retenir de la nomination des nouveaux mandataires publics en RDC ?","publisher":"Ebuteli","publication_date":"2022-09-09","url":"https://www.ebuteli.org/publications/podcasts/que-retenir-de-la-nomination-des-nouveaux-mandataires-publics-en-rdc/","claim":"Ebuteli argued that Tshisekedi's September 2022 public-enterprise appointments kept a patronage pattern alive, with managers often chosen for party membership or family/friend ties and some appointees lacking sector experience.","locator":"lines 37-48","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent Congolese research analysis that ties the appointments to a named ruling coalition and to specific selection criteria concerns, while remaining interpretive.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 target period.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to Tshisekedi's appointment power and coalition-management choices.","contrary_evidence":["This is an analytic podcast, not an audit of every appointee","the article frames some of the critique as inference about intent"],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC : de nouvelles nominations à la tête des établissements publics","publisher":"Radio Okapi","publication_date":"2022-11-16","url":"https://www.radiookapi.net/2022/11/16/actualite/politique/rdc-de-nouvelles-nominations-la-tete-des-etablissements-publics","claim":"Tshisekedi named leaders of multiple public entities and the CSAC, including political figures and insiders such as his economic adviser Marcellin Bilomba as director general of SONAHYDROC and other politically connected appointees.","locator":"lines 152-163","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct appointment notice with a detailed list of named appointees and office roles.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 target period.","ruler_attribution":"Direct: these were presidential appointments under Tshisekedi's formal authority.","contrary_evidence":["The appointment list alone does not prove patronage motive in every case","some named appointees had relevant professional backgrounds"],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"2022 Country Report on Human Rights Practices: Democratic Republic of the Congo","publisher":"U.S. Department of State","publication_date":"2023","url":"https://www.ecoi.net/en/document/2089109.html","claim":"The State Department reported that in June Tshisekedi dismissed several Supreme Audit Court magistrates for failing to pursue corruption cases and appointed new leadership, then swore in 57 magistrates in August; it also said the APLC operated under the Office of the President.","locator":"lines 271-275","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official U.S. government country report with specific, dated institutional actions and clear attribution to Tshisekedi.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 target period.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to Tshisekedi's authority over key accountability institutions.","contrary_evidence":["The same report says the audit court rarely published its findings","it also says the APLC record was mixed"],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC : l'APLC annonce avoir saisi une trentaine de camions des minerais et permis le recouvrement fiscal de plusieurs millions de USD dans le Lualaba au premier semestre 2022","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-07-07","url":"https://actualite.cd/index.php/2022/07/07/rdc-laplc-annonce-avoir-saisi-une-trentaine-de-camions-des-minerais-et-permis-le","claim":"The APLC said its Kolwezi team seized 33 trucks loaded with minerals and helped recover roughly 300 million dollars in fiscal revenue during the first half of 2022.","locator":"line 98","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Specific operational claim from the presidential anti-corruption agency, but still self-reported and not independently audited in the article.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 target period.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate to strong: the APLC is a presidential anti-corruption service operating under Tshisekedi's office.","contrary_evidence":["The figure is self-reported by the APLC","the article does not independently verify the recovered amount"],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC : Félix Tshisekedi encourage le gouvernement à récupérer le patrimoine immobilier de l’État acquis indûment par des tiers","publisher":"Radio Okapi","publication_date":"2022-09-17","url":"https://www.radiookapi.net/2022/09/17/actualite/politique/rdc-felix-tshisekedi-encourage-le-gouvernement-recuperer-le","claim":"At a Council of Ministers meeting, Tshisekedi urged the government to recover state real estate held or acquired unlawfully by third parties and to tighten controls on any disposition of state property.","locator":"lines 149-152","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous local reporting on a direct presidential instruction affecting public assets and anti-spoliation controls.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 target period.","ruler_attribution":"Direct: the instruction is attributed to Tshisekedi in his executive role.","contrary_evidence":["The source reports an instruction, not implementation","no independent recovery audit is provided here"],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.8","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Discours du Président de la République, Félix Tshisekedi sur l'état de la nation","publisher":"Présidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-12-10","url":"https://www.presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/discours_du_president_de_la_republique_felix_tshisekedi_sur_letat_de_la_nation","claim":"Tshisekedi presented the 2022 state-of-the-nation address as a duty of accountability and said the year's work covered anti-corruption, public revenue, elections preparation, and administrative modernization.","locator":"lines 72-75","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Direct self-statement from the president, but it is a summary of his own performance rather than an independent verification.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 target period.","ruler_attribution":"Direct self-statement by Tshisekedi.","contrary_evidence":["This is self-report rather than independent evaluation","it is framed as a positive annual roundup"],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC : Félix Tshisekedi nomme Jimmy Munganga Ngwaka, comme premier président de la cour des comptes","publisher":"Factuel","publication_date":"2022-07-01","url":"https://www.factuel.cd/2022/07/01/rdc-felix-tshisekedi-nomme-jimmy-munganga-ngwaka-comme-premier-president-de-la-cour-des","claim":"Tshisekedi appointed Jimmy Munganga Ngwaka to lead the Court of Accounts, which the article describes as an independent external controller of state finances and public entities.","locator":"lines 53-58","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Clear appointment notice with a direct description of the oversight role, though the independence claim is the article's framing rather than an observed outcome.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 target period.","ruler_attribution":"Direct presidential appointment power.","contrary_evidence":["The appointment alone does not prove the court's later independence in practice","the source is a secondary summary of the ordinance"],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC : Félix Tshisekedi ordene? no, actual citation omitted to preserve fidelity","publisher":"Presidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-12-10","url":"https://www.presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/discours_du_president_de_la_republique_felix_tshisekedi_sur_letat_de_la_nation","claim":"The 2022 state-of-the-nation address also framed the president's work as covering anti-corruption and public revenue, but the underlying evidence remains self-report and should be treated as such rather than independent verification.","locator":"lines 72-75","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Self-report with no external corroboration in the source itself.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"2022 target period.","ruler_attribution":"Direct self-statement by Tshisekedi.","contrary_evidence":["This is not independent evidence of execution","it overlaps with the retained official address item"],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.6","8B.10"]}

Gaps: the dossier is strongest on revealed goals, anti-corruption action, public-enterprise appointments, and crisis diplomacy. The main unresolved question is how far the repeated plans and summit outcomes translated into durable results rather than short-lived administrative motion.
